A||N||5||fierobaby||how do you put in new headlight motors?||||1||
Z||000000||fierobaby||06-22-2001||10:50 AM||||hey can I get some step by step on how to put in a new headlight motor? my father took mine out but I want to put the new one in  and surprise him... prove I can actually fix a car! so thanks for any help anyone can give me<P>Corinne<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://feiro.nl/uploads/cfiero1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by fierobaby (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-22-2001||10:52 AM||||they come out by removing just four nuts (10MM I think) and unplugging wires. They hold the whole assembly to the bulkhead. Then just wiggle it all out. You need the hood open. To put them back just place them back in and slide the mounting bracket over the 4 studs and put the nuts back on. plug in the wires.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||06-22-2001||10:54 AM||||DO NOT connect the power until your hands are clear. This thing can bite!||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierobaby||06-22-2001||10:55 AM||||LOL I know that all to well when we took it out I was the one by the headlight and ouch! it bit me damn thing!<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://feiro.nl/uploads/cfiero1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||06-22-2001||11:34 AM||||yes to that. disconnect your battery ground to be safe.||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||06-22-2001||01:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>they come out by removing just four nuts (10MM I think)...To put them back just place them back in and slide the mounting bracket over the 4 studs and put the nuts back on. plug in the wires.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just to clarify (probably unecessarily):  10mm is correct, for the HL motor nuts. <BR>Install one motor at a time.<P>Loosely install (2) nuts onto the lower studs in the car.  Next, crank the HL motor "down" (if it isn't already) and put the motor into place, slipping the motor over the 2 loose nuts you just pre-installed.  The motor assembly has slotted holes for the bottom two nuts, so the motor just slips over them.<P>Install the (2) upper nuts, then raise the HL (by hand - turn the knob until the headlight is fully up - approximately 1.5 billion turns  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ), reach down through the opened headlight assembly and tighten the lower nuts.  Finish off by tightening the upper two nuts again, and plugging in the connectors.  <P>As the others pointed out, keep your hands out of harm's way when you reconnect the motor(s)...  you'll probably want to use them again someday!  ||||reg||1
